Add a cargo-fuzz target `ndjson` (upstream has none)

A lean4export NDJSON stream checked as the arena's `pestka` entry runs
`bin/arena-run FILE 4` (susz pack --no-index, then pestka FILE.susz 4),
on one worker on the calling thread: packed in memory by susz 0.1.4 (the
arena's packer), then checked by the generated crate's `main` with
Aver's capability providers bound in the harness (Args: `export.susz 1`;
Disk: the packed bytes, read-only; Console: dropped). The crate is
generated with --single-thread (the native entry is multi-threaded; on
one worker the verdict is the same, and wasm32-wasip1 has no threads).
The providers are installed once per process and read the current
input, as wasmfuzz runs input after input in one instance (in-process
replays of the 226 arena fixtures give the per-process verdicts).
Every panic is a finding (main aborts on a panic: aver.toml panic =
"abort").
Upstream: none (no fuzz targets upstream; no issues, PR #1 is the
author's own, checked 2026-11-22).

